      "Language": "hun",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "Currently, peripheral arterial disease is an underdiagnosed disorder. Several modifiable and non-modifiable risk factors have role in its development and progression. As system disorder it might be a part and an important predictor of fatal cardio- and cerebrovascular events."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORT",
          "content": "The authors describe the case of a 73-year-old male with multilocational vascular disorder, with simultaneously occurring carotid disease, critical limb ischaemia with aorto-bifemoral bypass, multiple infarction with mechanical complication, inoperable coronary disease and with implantable cardioverter defibrillator for ventricular arrhythmia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Peripheral arterial disease affects the whole vascular system and can progress into serious cardiac and cerebral manifestations causing the patient's death inspite of comprehensive treatment."
        }
      ]},
